      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 The Author(s). Published by Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Michael N. Hall is this year's recipient of the Lasker Basic Medical Research Award for the identification of the target of rapamycin, TOR. TOR is a master regulator of the cell's growth and metabolic state, and its dysregulation contributes to a variety of diseases, including diabetes, obesity, neurodegenerative disorders, aging, and cancer, making the TOR pathway an attractive therapeutic target."
      },
